 "coverage_notes": "FRESH RUN (no prior checkpoint existed for 01/08/2026). Method: (1) The Tier-0 cache /Users/mangian/Downloads/BANKING/intel-cache/greek_tenders_diavgeia.json (286 below-threshold decisions, refreshed 01/08/2026) was fully triaged — a bank-fee/accounting filter leaves 269, a positive equipment-keyword filter leaves 68, of which roughly 20 are genuine ATM/POS/cash-automation/self-service procurements. Confirmed noise classes dropped: municipal 'ΛΟΓΙΣΤΙΚΗ ΤΑΚΤΟΠΟΙΗΣΗ / ΠΡΟΜΗΘΕΙΑ ΤΡΑΠΕΖΑΣ' card-acceptance fee postings (the single largest class), PVC pipe pressure ratings ('10 atm', '25 atm') at water utilities, air-traffic-management 'ATM/PALLAS 3G' at the Ministry of Infrastructure, the 'ATM Dubai' tourism trade fair at the Greek National Tourism Organisation, and self-service CAR WASH building permits at the Technical Chamber of Greece. (2) Every reported Diavgeia row was verified by downloading its own PDF from diavgeia.gov.gr/doc/<ADA> and extracting the text locally with pdfminer.six — nothing is reported on the strength of a cache subject line alone except the two corroborating rows explicitly flagged inside the off-site-ATM-siting signal (Zografou ΡΘ2ΛΩΡΦ-ΑΓΖ, Pogoniou 96ΜΣΩ1Ω-Υ1Π). (3) Beyond the cache, eleven further Diavgeia OpenData subject sweeps were run using deliberately fresh Greek terms the cache never used: μίσθωση χώρου ΑΤΜ, παραχώρηση χώρου ΑΤΜ, μηχανήματα αυτόματης ανάληψης, αυτόματων πωλητών εισιτηρίων, ταξινόμησης χαρτονομισμάτων, ανακυκλωτής χαρτονομισμάτων, χρηματαποστολών, διαχείρισης μετρητών, αυτόματο μηχάνημα πληρωμών, ηλεκτρονική ταυτοποίηση πελατών, ξεπλύματος χρήματος λογισμικό, έξυπνο χρηματοκιβώτιο. These produced the four findings the cache had missed entirely: the ODAP ticket-vending-machine study, the Mykonos ATM enforcement decision, the Chalkida ATM request and the Athens 36-month cash-transport tender revocation. (4) Bank of Greece, ELTA and Tameio Parakatathikon & Daneion were each checked on their own sites; the TPD procurement page lists no cash-handling tender, confirming that its counting machines go by direct award. GENUINE GAPS: KIMDIS/ESIDIS above-threshold notices were NOT searched directly — promitheus.gov.gr was not reachable through the fetch tool available in this run, so above-threshold Greek notices are covered only indirectly via Diavgeia commitment decisions and the separate TED cache; a dedicated ESIDIS sweep is the top priority for the next run. Greek commercial banks (Piraeus, Alpha, Eurobank, NBG) publish no procurement notices because they are private and outside Diavgeia, so their ATM/POS spend is structurally invisible on this portal — that is itself the finding, and it mirrors the 'Croatian commercial banks: NONE FOUND' result from the aborted 31/07 run. Notably, sweeps for banknote RECYCLERS (ανακυκλωτής) and banknote SORTING (ταξινόμησης) returned ZERO results anywhere in the Greek public sector over the last six months: Greek public buyers are still buying simple counters and counterfeit detectors, not recycling or sorting equipment.",
 "access_issues": "api.diavgeia.gov.gr does not resolve from this host (DNS ENOTFOUND) via either Bash or WebFetch, so the documented Diavgeia JSON API route was unavailable; the working substitute is https://diavgeia.gov.gr/opendata/search.json?subject=<term> for listing and https://diavgeia.gov.gr/doc/<ADA> for the document itself. Bash has NO network access on this host at all, so every fetch had to go through WebFetch. Diavgeia serves binary PDFs that the fetch tool cannot read, but it does save them to disk, and pdfminer.six (v20260107, present) extracts them cleanly — system pdftotext is NOT installed. www.bankofgreece.gr/enimerosi/prokhryxeis returns HTTP 404; the live route is the announcements search at /enimerosi/grafeio-typoy/anazhthsh-enhmerwsewn. The source-catalogue hint of filtering Diavgeia by q=organizationUid:100000602 does NOT work through this route — it returns the entire 3.1m-decision corpus unfiltered, so per-organisation Diavgeia filtering should be treated as untested rather than tested_ok. The metaforespress.gr article on ELTA banking services returned HTTP 404. promitheus.gov.gr (KIMDIS/ESIDIS) was not reachable. Claude-in-Chrome is not connected in this run. Operational note for the harness: the shared scratchpad directory is written concurrently by sibling country agents and a helper module written there was overwritten mid-run by another agent's file of the same name — country agents should use a per-agent subdirectory.",
 "operator_requests": "1) The ELTA 2026-2030 Development Plan document itself, with its investment/capex annex — presented to staff on 24/07/2026 and so far only summarised in press. It is the highest-value document on the Greek beat and decides whether ELTA 'financial services' means cash/ATM infrastructure or agency banking only; likely obtainable from ELTA investor relations or the Growthfund (Superfund). 2) ELTA Supply Contract F.P. 6276/2016 with BOOS S.A., which still governs CashDNA TN10 labour and parts pricing in 2026 — needed to establish its expiry date and whether it is exclusive. 3) A KIMDIS/ESIDIS (promitheus.gov.gr) above-threshold sweep for Greek CPVs 30123600, 35121200, 30234000 and 50310000, which this run could not reach."
